  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000003">
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Biospecimen: A material sample taken from a biological entity for testing, diagnostic, propagation, treatment or research purposes, including a sample obtained from a living organism or taken from the biological object after halting of all its life functions.</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Biospecimen: A material entity that derives from an anatomical part or substance arising from an organism, and bears the role that is gained during a biospecimen collection activity and that can be realized by using it in a study</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/specimen"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2075980"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://bioschemas.org/Sample"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/MaterialSample"/>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C70699"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">biosample</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">specimen</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Any material sample taken from a biological entity for testing, diagnostic, propagation, treatment or research purposes, including a sample obtained from a living organism or taken from the biological object after halting of all its life functions. Biospecimen can contain one or more components including but not limited to cellular molecules, cells, tissues, organs, body fluids, embryos, and body excretory products.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nf16dcadaea7d44ac9083de69b208aef5"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q485146"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C70699"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-05-08) The session focused on defining "biospecimen" in the context of pharmaceutical R&amp;ED. Three definitions were considered. The expert group agreed on key scoping principles: The concept applies specifically to R&amp;ED in pharma. It explicitly excludes purely physical-chemical specimens or samples not derived from biological entities, thereby providing necessary conceptual precision. The concept broadly aligns with "sample" but is more targeted and appropriate for biomedical research involving biological material. The NCIT_C70699 definition was the convergence candidate, recommended by three partner organizations and endorsed by (Peter McQuilton) and (Birgit Meldal). It was considered both comprehensive and appropriately scoped for PGO use. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on NCIT_C70699. Formal recommendation submitted to the Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000003</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">biospecimen</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">biospecimen</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ndf5e1bef3d014e279439fd735db6d60a"/>
  </rdf:Description>
