  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000031">
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">cell line: A cell line is a collection of genetically identical cells. [http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010054]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Cell Line: A permanently established cell culture that will proliferate indefinitely given appropriate fresh medium and space. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C16403]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Cell Line: Established cell cultures that have the potential to propagate indefinitely. [https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/M0003757.html]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nbcb7f95f7c844af0934881f2402a24fa"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nc2b8b39317c74d7ea796910c481447b5"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N85919822fd0e4fe7808a247bdba4e01c"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A cultured cell population that represents a genetically stable and homogeneous population that shares a common propagation history.</skos:definition>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Cell culture line</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Established cell line</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Cultured cell line</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">cell line</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cell line</rdfs:label>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-08</prov:endedAtTime>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000031</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLO_0000031"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">Cell Line Ontology (CLO). Definition of Cell Line. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLO_0000031</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nc5f39bbfcd6640aaaa069bd30af3ec65"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N74cf0de2a8284b00841f8a6413c896bd"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2026-04-23) The session reviewed four candidate definitions for Cell_Line, from the Cell Line Ontology (CLO), the Semanticscience Integrated Ontology (SIO), the National Cancer Institute Thesaurus (NCIT) and Medical Subject Headings (MeSH). The experts rejected the SIO definition because "genetically identical" is too strict: cell lines drift genetically across passages. They rejected the NCIT definition because not all cell lines proliferate indefinitely (primary cell lines, for example, stop after a limited number of divisions). They found that the MeSH definition lacks any genetic component. The group agreed that the CLO definition is the closest available option. Experts flagged one limitation: the phrase "shares a common propagation history" may not fit commercially distributed cell lines bought from several vendors. One expert noted that propagation history can branch like a tree while still having a common ancestor. The same expert proposed an adapted text anchored in Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) terms, which the group recorded as a candidate improvement to submit to CLO rather than as a PGO definition. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on the CLO definition (CLO_0000031). Label `Cell_Line` confirmed. The Pistoia Alliance will propose an improvement to the CLO maintainers to cover commercially distributed cell lines.</dcterms:description>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLO_0000031"/>
  </rdf:Description>
