  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000006">
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">clinical study site</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A healthcare organization, an institution, a facility, a healthcare provider, or a part or a constituent of any of the above entities directly involved in conducting a particular clinical study.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000006</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Study Site: A facility in which study/protocol activities are conducted. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C80403]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Site: A place, setting, or context in which something is situated or to which something is, or may be, bound. [https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/20250201/Facilities/Site]</skos:editorialNote>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C70777"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/Place"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MedicalOrganization"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Site"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q57951700"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">clinical study site</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/394577000"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C70777"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N3e69d0dddd084178b64773a2ce655495"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N599d2ce7ab9a43a4961b3a6462118cf2"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nad2576b7f89c4cc7b80d35bd4bacf4c0"/>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-01-30) The session revealed significant conceptual complexity around the term "site", which spans anatomical, geographic, institutional, and procedural domains. Experts distinguished between a high-level generic concept and more context-specific subtypes. Key findings: **BFO_0000029 (Site)**: Philosophically rigorous but too abstract for practical PGO implementation. Some experts appreciated its generality; others considered it impractical. **OMG Site definition** ("place, setting, or context in which something is situated or to which something is, or may be, bound") was generally preferred by experts for its clarity and pragmatic scope — however, the IRI is unresolvable (issue #48), blocking immediate adoption. **NCIT_C70777 (Clinical Study Site)**: Strongly endorsed for representing real-world entities engaged in clinical research. The experts recommended a stratified approach: 1. A generic "Site" — pending a resolvable URI for the OMG definition. 2. "Clinical_Study_Site" (NCIT_C70777) — adopt for Phase 1. 3. Additional Phase 2 concepts: "Study_Site", "Anatomical_Site", "Binding_Site". **Outcome:** Further update required to confirm OMG IRI status and finalise the pragmatic recommendation. **Round 2** (2025-05-28) Follow-up confirmed that the OMG IRI issue (#48) could not be resolved: OMG IRIs are not currently resolvable, per input from Asiyah Yu Lin (Pistoia Alliance). As a consequence, the OMG "Site" definition cannot be used for PGO at this time. The pragmatic proposal for Phase 1: 1. Defer a generic "Site" definition until a resolvable and implementable URI is available. 2. Adopt "Clinical_Study_Site" with NCIT_C70777 as the Phase 1 core concept. 3. Flag additional Phase 2 sub-concepts for subsequent alignment. **Outcome:** Final recommendation confirmed. Submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N4131c8fe988142a9bad8bbce68ed31d2"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000018">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N52470e30689548d9ac3f1ef0735a2bcb"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N384aecb00ee14eeca2204aa50cf0ee4c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N3c87a1514e5f4a64926e7b340e253bb5"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">AdverseEvent: An event that may be related to unintended effects on a patient or research participant. [https://www.hl7.org/fhir/adverseevent.html]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Adverse Event: Pathologic Function type from UMLS [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MEDDRA]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Adverse Event Actuality: Overall nature of the adverse event, e.g. real or potential. [https://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-adverse-event-actuality.html]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Adverse Event: An unfavorable change in the health of a participant, including abnormal laboratory findings, that happens during a clinical study or within a certain period of time after the study. [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/CTO-NDD]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Synonym 'Adverse drug reaction': AE subset</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">AdverseEvent: Any unfavorable and unintended sign, symptom, disease, or other medical occurrence with a temporal association with the use of a medical product, procedure, or other medical intervention. [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/BRIDG]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">adverse effect: [Specification of] any potential undesirable side effect, adverse reaction or event, complication, or other similar potential consequence associated with the use of a medicinal product. [(URL not provided)]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Unwanted effect</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Side effect</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Adverse drug reaction</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Adverse effect</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C41331"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N78e91ac3c116473ca605b3de1d3f0696"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N3c12c29da47c48eb8d81b817ff056526"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">NCI Thesaurus, National Cancer Institute. Concept C41331. https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C41331</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000018</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">adverse event</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">adverse event</rdfs:label>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C41331"/>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-03-03</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Any unfavorable or unintended disease, sign, or symptom (including an abnormal laboratory finding) that is temporally associated with the use of a medical treatment or procedure, and that may or may not be considered related to the medical treatment or procedure.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-10-16) The session (2025-10-16) focused on Adverse Event as the primary concept (Medical Device was also discussed — separate record another concept). The group reviewed approximately 10 candidate definitions, removing exact duplicates during the call. The shortlist converged on two candidates: OAE_0000001 and NCIT C41331. OAE_0000001 was judged concise and from an authoritative dedicated ontology for adverse events, but noted as potentially limited in scope and not updated since 2022. NCIT C41331 was preferred by the group for its content richness — it covers drug-drug interactions (noted by an expert: "takes into account drug-drug interaction as well"), applies across clinical, regulatory, and post-market contexts, and is from a highly trusted, broadly used source. Darko noted NCIT definitions are generally "wordy" but agreed on content quality. Process issues also discussed: URL policy established: definitions must point to the original source organization, not BioPortal. BioPortal is acceptable for discovery but not as the primary citation. Ammar added SIDER (http://sideeffects.embl.de/) as an example resource for Adverse Event during the call. A "meta-level" context label (R&amp;D vs. clinical) was requested by Chris Day and an expert, but noted by Giovanni as requiring an agreed pharma meta-model not yet available. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on NCIT C41331 as the preferred definition with the label `Adverse_Event`. Formal recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nccb4d65d5ac2436f94b5341f10069f22">
    <void:uriSpace>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/</void:uriSpace>
