  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000012">
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2024-09-11) The session reviewed six candidate definitions for "indication". Several definitions were immediately excluded due to the absence of a resolvable URI. Two candidates remained viable: 1. **NCIT_C41184** — provides a resolvable IRI with CC BY 4.0 license. 2. **CDISC Glossary** — the CDISC definition is preferred by some experts for its clarity ("A health problem or disease that is identified as likely to be benefited by a therapy..."), but CDISC reuses the NCIT code C41184 with its own wording, and no separate URI exists for the CDISC-specific definition. Discussion notes: "Abnormal" or "pathological" are unnecessarily restrictive when defining indication. The distinction between sign and symptom in the NCIT definition was noted. NCIT code C41184 may be acceptable, with all alternate definitions treated as equally valid. The group reached consensus: adopt NCIT_C41184 as the primary definition, with all listed alternate definitions acknowledged as equally valid. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C41184 as primary definition, CDISC definition as alternative label. Submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
