  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000008">
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">device: A material entity that is designed to perform a function in a scientific investigation, but is not a reagent. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000968]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Medical Device: Any physical object that is useful for prevention, diagnosis, monitoring, or treatment of disease or other conditions. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16830]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">medical device: Specification of an instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, material or other article ... not achieve its principal intended action by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means ... [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11615-MedicinalProducts/MedicalDevice]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6554101"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C62103"/>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000008</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">instrument</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">laboratory instrument</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">device</skos:prefLabel>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Device"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6554101"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://bioschemas.org/Thing"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Device"/>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An object contrived for a specific purpose. OR: An object that has a specific use. In medicine, wheelchairs, pumps, and artificial limbs are examples of devices.</skos:definition>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N40cc3b5bb8c94a6c99c15cc2614c84ea"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Ndeb1912d11364f37bb49afb4723afd23"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">device</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C62103"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N702cd0a7d2d143c1a8ce57d09d6acda3"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N6446936e587044f696784ddb7f24c9fc"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-02-13) There is a need for a broad "device" core concept in pharma R&amp;ED. The variety of devices deployed in pharma is enormous, so context is important. Key discussion points: "Device" makes sense as a high-level entry-point label; covers laboratory equipment, production equipment, diagnostic tools, and medical devices. NCIT_C62103 (*"An object contrived for a specific purpose"*) was considered pragmatically appropriate despite some concern about breadth. An additional option was noted: NCIT_C19238 (*"A manufactured object used to perform diagnostic, therapeutic or research activities"*) — would exclude manufacturing equipment. IDMP-O's "medical device" definition is appropriate as a future sub-concept child class. The group reached consensus on NCIT_C62103 for the Phase 1 "device" concept, with three sub-concepts recommended for Phase 2: "Instrument" — laboratory/measurement device for scientific investigation "Medical device" — e.g. NCIT_C16830 "Manufacturing equipment" — tablet manufacturing device (out of scope for R&amp;ED extension) GitHub issue #37 remains open pending a formal label decision in the PGO repository. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C62103. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000017">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A unit of measure, or unit, is a particular quantity value that has been chosen as a scale for measuring other quantities the same kind (more generally of equivalent dimension). For example, the meter is a quantity of length that has been rigorously defined and standardized by the BIPM (International Board of Weights and Measures). Any measurement of the length can be expressed as a number multiplied by the unit meter. More formally, the value of a physical quantity Q with respect to a unit (U) is expressed as the scalar multiple of a real number (n) and U, as Q=nU.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-03-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N854720de9ab74ce49d4f1885d5800104"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N98d91c30ebd74855ad750b35812cb940"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N89a5c5b795f24e31bb7eaccadc331cd1"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2024-10-24) The definitions were considered quite similar across candidates. A preference was stated for the QUDT unit definition for accuracy and precision. The QUDT definition is also used in the CMC Process Ontology (Pistoia), which imports QUDT for quantities and units. The proposal: adopt the QUDT_unit definition as the PGO "unit" definition, unless there is conflicting input from the CMC Process Ontology (there was none). **Outcome:** Preliminary consensus on QUDT. Additional expert input requested from IDMP-O team.</dcterms:description>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Unit of Measure: A named quantity in terms of which other quantities are measured or specified, used as a standard measurement of like kinds. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C25709]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">unit of measurement: The definite magnitude of a physical quantity or of time. It has a quantity and a unit associated with it. [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/bao/classes/http%253A%252F%252Fwww.bioassayontology.org%252Fbao%2523BAO_0000077]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">measurement unit: Real scalar quantity, defined and adopted by convention, with which any other quantity of the same kind can be compared to express the ratio of the second quantity to the first one as a number. [https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/QuantitiesAndUnits/MeasurementUnit]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">unit of measurement: A unit of measurement is a definite magnitude of a physical quantity, defined and adopted by convention and/or by law, that is used as a standard for measurement of the same physical quantity. [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/sio/classes/http%253A%252F%252Fsemanticscience.org%252Fresource%252FSIO_000074]</skos:editorialNote>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">unit</rdfs:label>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N60f41da9e2464d499ca1d099d75f43aa"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N68052d1feeed438a8c0afcbc4450ab74"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N2b7b7a4a9b004476ae46564968c2be07"/>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000017</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"/>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"QUDT is published under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. © QUDT.org Contributors."</dcterms:rights>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">unit</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N032d7975c4b1493c877eac7c6ada90fa">
    <dcterms:title>FDA Drugs@FDA</dcterms:title>
