  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000032">
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N05e55fc75b8d4b66ba7bfedfc6646504"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N7d4db4e4b93347f386d5737d7e939d64"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nf79b9ecaef004d79af512b16a8db3a0b"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0000324"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Cell category</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Cell class</skos:altLabel>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">Experimental Factor Ontology (EFO). Definition of Cell Type. http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0000324</dcterms:rights>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0000324"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ne699cb7eff0948fd9faf7e20e219447d"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Na952e657df4f4babb6c03a30d3d2f1ca"/>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">cell type</skos:prefLabel>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2026-04-23) The session compared two candidate definitions for Cell_Type, from the Cell Ontology (CL) and the Experimental Factor Ontology (EFO). The experts rejected the CL definition by consensus as hard to understand and too arbitrary in how it groups cells. The discussion raised a modeling point: a cell type is a descriptor of a cell (a class), not a material entity, which matters for placement in ontologies aligned with Basic Formal Ontology (BFO). All experts accepted the EFO definition, "a distinct morphological or functional form of cell" (examples: epithelial cell, glial cell). The group chose not to add detail, because a more specific wording could exclude valid instances. The question of when to name a concept with the suffix "type" (cell type, tissue type) was noted as an open modeling topic for later phases. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on the EFO definition (EFO_0000324). Label `Cell_Type` confirmed.</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cell type</rdfs:label>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-08</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A distinct morphological or functional form of cell.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000032</dcterms:identifier>
