    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">cell type: A cell type is a distinct morphological or functional form of cell. Examples of criteria that can be used to define a cell type include: ploidy, nuclei number, layers, functional role, response to signals, typical metabolic profile, location, and biomarkers. [CL (Cell Ontology)]</skos:editorialNote>
