  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000007">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">chemical</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">chemical substance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">chemical compound</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nfb418300ac724bbb8b59f7921d04a16c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nb1e3d9b50122472986e99eb93d6e7f6d"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Na231f74caf3d40f0919e58ee7a86e7d9"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nbae414aa21b74ce0a660ecdc82750285"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N8078439a06dc4600945bb8809c0f567a"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N8e98e563d80c4911aa5fdb25e2139e91"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N2c961191a5154ccbb71d274e524eaf5c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N48ad3840ba6f42eb80077faa7106a9d4"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">compound</rdfs:label>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N3880403362864bddb1a5b0c3a875984f"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N0ed0d2bd6b164bfd929835fed3027745"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Neb2d29cf6ada4d2aa697b54eed748b62"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N928bfd1a2b96476d86fd1945fa7dbc5c"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N2b74f55a8c2a400eaa2d03f2f5c58428"/>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Substance"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ChemicalSubstance"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A substance formed by chemical union of two or more elements or ingredients in definite proportion by weight.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">compound</skos:prefLabel>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000007</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Substances_Hydrate: Description of the addition of a compound (substance) that contains water in weak chemical combination with another compound [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11238-Substances/Hydrate]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Chemical substance: A chemical substance is a portion of matter of constant composition, composed of molecular entities of the same type or of different types. [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:59999]</skos:editorialNote>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-03-06) The session jointly evaluated "Compound" and "Substance" to clarify their conceptual relationship. Key findings: "Compound" appears to have a more precise, accurate chemical composition than "Substance"; "Chemical compound" was noted as a possibly more accurate label but compatible with NCIT_C43366. The semantic boundaries between "compound", "substance", "drug", and "product" were acknowledged as context-dependent and partially overlapping. Initial convergence on NCIT_C43366 as the least controversial definition. **Outcome:** Initial consensus on NCIT_C43366. Follow-up session scheduled. **Round 2** (2025-03-25) The round 2 session confirmed NCIT_C43366 as the least controversial candidate. The group acknowledged the definition is not ideal — "substance", "element", and "ingredient" are imprecise terms — but no better candidate with a resolvable identifier and permissive licence was identified. The label "compound" was confirmed as appropriate (over "chemical compound"), aligned with common pharma R&amp;D usage. The group also discussed examples to illustrate the distinction between compound, drug, and product: acetylsalicylic acid (as compound) vs. aspirin (as product) acetaminophen (as compound) vs. paracetamol (as product) semaglutide (as compound/drug) **Outcome:** Consensus confirmed on NCIT_C43366. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C43366"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ChemicalEntity"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43366"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11173"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
  </rdf:Description>
