  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000013">
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N7b0fed86bf34407ab0f6ecad20aa8afc"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N14b04d1a834a4313b0236f08d2f13897"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Product: Something that is produced by, results from, or obtained as a consequence of some process or transformation. [https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/ProductsAndServices/Product]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Medicinal product: A substance or combination of substances that is intended to treat, prevent or diagnose a disease, or to restore, correct or modify physiological functions by exerting a pharmacological, immunological or metabolic action. [(IDMP)]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Pharmaceutical Product: A portion of manufactured substance that contains one or more biologically active and/or biologically inactive substances, intended to treat, prevent or alleviate the symptoms of disease or abnormal condition. [https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004364.html]</skos:editorialNote>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N032d7975c4b1493c877eac7c6ada90fa"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N1bb5347f14714f29ae9b4061172e0f2d"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-05-23) The session was conducted as a joint evaluation with "compound" and "substance" to clarify conceptual boundaries. Key discussion points: **Label**: Steering Committee recommendation (Cambridge 2025) to use "Pharmaceutical_Product" rather than "Product" was endorsed. **IDMP-O**: Definitions based on ISO standards, not publicly identifiable; confirmed not appropriate for PGO (GitHub issue #54, closed 2025-05). **CDISC/NCIT_C42639**: The CDISC definition (*"Qualitative and quantitative composition of a medicinal product in the dose form authorized..."*) resolvable via NCIT_C42639 and preferred by the expert group. **Should medical devices be included?** The group noted that implanted hips, digital medical devices, and companion diagnostics are not covered by the adopted definition. May warrant a broader core concept in a future PGO phase. **Relevance for R&amp;ED**: The concept must be addressed in early development, not only commercial operations. The group opted for the CDISC definition resolvable via NCIT_C42639. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C42639/CDISC definition. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000013</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C42639"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">drug</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical substance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">product</skos:altLabel>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_23888"/>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Medication"/>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Drug"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Qualitative and quantitative composition of a medicinal product in the dose form authorized by the regulatory authority for administration to patients, and as represented with any corresponding regulated product information. NOTE: A medicinal product may contain one or more pharmaceutical products. In many instances, the pharmaceutical product is the manufactured item. However, there are instances where the manufactured item undergoes further preparation before being administered to the patient (as the pharmaceutical product).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical product</skos:prefLabel>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q28885102"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO11615-MedicinalProducts/PharmaceuticalProduct/PharmaceuticalProduct"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical product</rdfs:label>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
  </rdf:Description>
