  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000022">
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N78752d99dc9945d7bd619ccee704a484"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nec3c485200d7453c83c5e35cc9d5833c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nfe02df4a9aa04136a1c3804f17dc10d5"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N433334a15cd54d9089511be62d968fc2"/>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Contra-indication</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Adverse Event (context): Any unfavorable or unintended disease, sign, or symptom … temporally associated with the use of a medical treatment. [NCIT:C41331]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Contraindication: situation where the medicinal product shall not be given for safety reasons [ISO IDMP]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Contraindications: A condition or factor associated with a recipient that makes the use of a drug, procedure, or physical agent improper or inadvisable. Contraindications may be absolute (life threatening) or relative (higher risk of complications in which benefits may outweigh risks). [http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000075202]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Medical Contraindication: A symptom or medical condition that makes a particular treatment or procedure inadvisable because a person is likely to have a bad reaction. For example, having a bleeding disorder is a contraindication for taking aspirin because treatment with aspirin may cause excess bleeding. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C50646]</skos:editorialNote>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055"/>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">contraindication</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contraindication</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The session reviewed multiple candidate definitions for Contraindication, including sources from OAE, MeSH, NCIT, and ISO IDMP. The group examined the conceptual relationship between Contraindication and Adverse Event — explicitly distinguishing the two: an adverse event is what may occur, while a contraindication is the reason not to proceed with a treatment. The OAE definition (OAE_0000055) emerged as the clear preference: Darko Hric noted it offers "more descriptive language than others while keeping it precise"; Birgit Meldal agreed. The group acknowledged a mild wording issue — the phrase "An contraindication" contains a grammatical error (should be "A contraindication") and the definition has a degree of circularity — but these were deemed non-blocking. The MeSH definition (absolute/relative split) was considered but judged as less precise. The NCIT C50646 definition was noted as qualitatively good but would require a label change. The ISO IDMP definition was rejected for being too drug-centric. Post-session, the Steering Group confirmed the label as the single word "contraindication" (rejecting the hyphenated form "contra-indication") and requested an optional improvement: consider submitting an updated definition to OAE to reduce circularity. This optional action was flagged 2026-05-28; no status change was triggered. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on OAE OAE_0000055 as the preferred definition. Label `Contraindication` confirmed.</dcterms:description>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-03-03</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N71c6c64cccb24da3a65abf0bfcdeebe9"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ne2e8b0ceedb14d9ea66df636129c991a"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000022</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">Ontology of Adverse Events, OAE_0000055. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A contraindication is a disposition that increases the risk of harm involved in using a particular drug, carrying out a medical procedure, or engaging in a particular activity such that the risk of harm exceeds a threshold. An contraindication serves as a reason to withhold a certain medical treatment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
  </rdf:Description>
