  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000027">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">medical indication</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">Schema.org. Term: MedicalIndication. https://schema.org/MedicalIndication</dcterms:rights>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Therapeutic Indication: Therapeutic indications are a description of the disease to be treated with a medicine, and the population for which the medicine is intended. [EUPATI Toolbox (no persistent URI)]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Indication: A sign, signal, circumstance, or symptom which serves to indicate or point out the cause, pathology, treatment, or issue of an attack of disease; the basis for initiation of a treatment for a disease or of a diagnostic test. [NCIT:C41184]</skos:editorialNote>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nccb4d65d5ac2436f94b5341f10069f22"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N04fdf2b1c4164ce689406ee4483f631d"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ne264e3f194aa49ecb83873c6ff623c34"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MedicalIndication"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A condition or factor that indicates use of a medical therapy, including signs, symptoms, risk factors, anatomical states, etc.</skos:definition>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000027</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Therapeutic indication</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Clinical indication</skos:altLabel>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N7011184d6a9a48cc8ef1c754e80f244c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N7f4857ad63dd470295c685cf64d8c77d"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nce95290b67be4faf94d3b224f62dde60"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">medical indication</skos:prefLabel>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MedicalIndication"/>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The alignment sessions (2025-11-14 and 2025-11-26) explored the scope of Therapeutic/Medical Indication as a specialisation of Indication (PGO V1.0). The group noted that no single available definition was fully satisfactory: "There is no fully satisfactory candidate. A combination of the wording from e.g. https://schema.org/MedicalIndication and e.g. https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q496997 would be preferred." The NCIT C41184 definition (already used for PGO V1.0 Indication) was excluded for re-use here. The EUPATI Toolbox definition was broadly rejected as drug-centric and lacking a persistent identifier. Wikipedia was qualitatively appreciated but rejected for instability. Schema.org MedicalIndication emerged as the preferred primary source: Ammar Ammar proposed it; an expert noted its conciseness; Birgit Meldal endorsed it for including risk factors (relevant for vaccine indications); an expert found it "less verbose and more focused"; Philippe Rocca-Serra and Ammar Ammar gave explicit +1. Wikidata Q496997 was strongly endorsed as a complementary framing (Birgit Meldal, Philippe Rocca-Serra) but was not selected as primary given stability concerns. A key label discussion emerged: the group strongly felt that "Therapeutic_Indication" is too narrow — it excludes diagnostic indications and prevention scenarios. The proposal to change the label to "Medical_Indication" was put forward during the 2025-11-26 session and confirmed by the SG at 2026-05-13 (ISSUE I-02). The meeting notes record: "Medical Indication is broader than Therapeutic Indication." The relationship to PGO V1.0 Indication was discussed: Medical_Indication is likely a child entity of Indication, with a more specific therapy-oriented scope. This modelling point was not formally resolved at the expert level. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on schema.org MedicalIndication as the preferred definition. Label changed to `Medical_Indication`. SG approval: 2026-05-13. Editorial note: definition may need future refinement incorporating Wikidata Q496997 wording.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-05-13</prov:endedAtTime>
  </rdf:Description>
