    <dcterms:title>Protein Ontology (PRO)</dcterms:title>
    <skos:note>PRO (PRotein Ontology). Protein-coding genes are organised under the sequence_feature -&gt; protein_coding_gene (SO:0001217) branch: 88,000+ genes across species, each cross-referenced to a species gene DB (human -&gt; HGNC, rat -&gt; RGD, chicken -&gt; CGNC, etc.). Added on an expert's suggestion (2026-09-15); verified 2026-10-19. Gene classes reuse the source-DB IRI as their identifier, so cite via the OLS4 PRO class page</skos:note>
    <sh:pattern>PR:[0-9]+</sh:pattern>
  </rdf:Description>
